WEBVTT

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.390
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:27.980
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.400
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.820
Things never get any better.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.740
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.040
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.510
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.260
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.390
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:10.150
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.110
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.450
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:22.030
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:28.540
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.260
The Social Rehabilitation Promotion Centre.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:41.140
It's one of the prisons that were built
through that private sector initiative.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.390
Not unlike myself, most of the people
imprisoned there are first-time offenders.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:51.020
My speech during the war was labelled as being in
violation of the New Information Privacy Protection Act;

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.650
I was imprisoned there until last week.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:58.410
If I remember correctly, Yajima-san, you were Kaishou Rinroku's...

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.470
I'm a friend of his from back in college.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:07.710
I became a critic... though he tended toward a more technical field.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.710
Yet you're asking for Shinjuurou's help?

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.040
A trap! It's a trap!

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.300
I can't ask Kaishou.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:19.260
As a matter of fact, I can only trust you two, who stand in opposition to him.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:23.760
Yajima-sensei.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.520
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:30.500
I thought I would get the chance to meet you here.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.020
I heard that your stomach hasn't been feeling well.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.240
Yes...

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.690
...thanks to that, my release date has been moved up.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.400
I have something I'd like you to look at.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.350
Book: A History of Criminal Psychology

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.800
This is one of my personal possessions...

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.370
This is quite the rare book.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.030
I actually have a copy myself.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.460
Well, well...

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:53.620
I wonder... does that say Kaishou Rinroku?

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:55.090
There's no doubt about it.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.100
Where did you get this?

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.720
At a used book store before I was brought here.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.590
Would you mind if I held onto this?

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.850
I'd love to show it to Kaishou and see the look on his face.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:11.730
Especially since it would be damaging to his reputation, should it become public that his personal books were on the market.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.230
But of course.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.590
Thank you.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.200
Well then...

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.490
The fact that you're here must mean... is there something ailing you as well?

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.180
It's right here.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.630
It's right here, Sensei.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.050
Right here...

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.130
That man gave you this piece of paper?

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.880
No. It was most likely stuck between the pages of this book originally.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.390
I know this because...

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.970
...it has the printed label of my personalised writing paper.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.380
This is my writing paper.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:56.270
So then... you wrote this?

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.180
Certainly not.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.900
This is a book from Kaishou Rinroku's personal collection after all.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:05.520
Why was a piece of my writing paper stuck between the pages?

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:09.930
So the reason you hired me is to solve that mystery?

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:12.730
Furthermore, why was it within this particular book?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:14.200
That's all?

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.470
I want to know everything you find out.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.290
Why don't you just ask Kaishou-san directly?!

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:22.040
I can't imagine he'd answer me truthfully.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.630
Excuse me...

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.050
Why don't we examine the fingerprints on it?

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.590
W-Who is this girl?

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.840
Can you do it?

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.560
If I can get something electronic, I can manage it.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:34.750
You have a cell phone, right?

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:41.100
Oh! I can feel it! I can feel it!

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.050
Bring me the paper.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.030
Okay!

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.430
She's not human, is she?

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.000
She's human.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.340
She's a R.A.I.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:57.880
R.A.I.?

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.870
I thought they were banned...

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:08.720
I was able to detect two separate sets of fingerprints matching what was registered with the police dept.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.510
One of those was Yajima-san's.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:12.790
The other was-

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:13.970
Kaishou Rinroku, right?

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.270
Yajima Takako.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.820
Yajima?

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.150
She's my wife...

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:23.920
I suppose it makes sense that your wife
would sometimes handle your writing paper.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.780
Ah... I guess you're right.

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:32.790
Ah! She broke it, she broke it! Kazamori broke it!

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.790
When I broke through security, I accidentally overloaded it.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:37.040
Hey, Shinjuurou! Kazamori broke it!

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:42.920
So Yajima Takako's fingerprints are in the Metropolitan Police Dept's database...

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:44.680
What are you gonna do?

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.920
This could turn out to be interesting...

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.930
...if we can catch that Kaishou by the tail, that is.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.970
Are you gonna feed me... Kaishou's soul?

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.980
"34-14-14"...

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:02.360
Could this be...

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:08.030
...the 14th character in the 14th column of page 34?

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:12.270
If that's the case, the first character would be "i".

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.360
The next one is... "tsu".

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.630
And then... "mo"!

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:20.080
See?! It's starting to look like a sentence!

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.170
Let's see, the next character is...

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.760
"I'll be at the usual place"...?

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.760
I went ahead and saved you some time.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:33.590
What's with you?!

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:35.600
If you've already deciphered it, tell me already!

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.780
I wouldn't even call it a code.

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:41.060
It's far too simple and straightforward.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:45.840
Nonetheless, if the paper and book were to be separated, no one would be able to decode it.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.670
That's certainly true...

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.860
And so... why was this paper in my father's book?

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.870
That's what I'd like to know.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:55.970
"I'll be at the usual place"...

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.960
Could it be a means of coordinating a rendezvous?

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.620
But something like this could easily be relayed through a call or text.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.000
Maybe they couldn't meet with this person if the method of contact left a record.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.880
Are you trying to suggest the writer is involved in something criminal?

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:07.980
No...

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:12.300
By the way, your mother is...

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.630
She died when I was three years old.

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:16.150
Why ask me that all of a sudden?

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:16.680
It's nothing...

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.150
Well, I see...

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:22.360
By the way, where is that Inga woman right now?

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:23.560
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.070
Here are your crepes.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:29.110
Now, don't you dare start complaining about how it's not sweet.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:31.820
Even though it's a crepe, it's a proper meal.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:35.200
I figured you've been eating nothing but junk lately, so I decided to invite you to lunch.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:39.080
Long ago, parts of Southeast Asia were colonised by France.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.830
I've had these more times than I can count.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:50.510
A used bookstore?

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:51.670
There's simply no way...

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:53.930
...that book is still within this house.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:55.680
Um...

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.060
Hey, where was it again?

00:07:58.480 --> 00:07:59.810
Is this the one?

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.060
Ah, that's it!

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:06.190
They look exactly the same, but does that mean it's a fake?

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:07.600
It would have to be.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.980
If you could make someone believe that it came from Kaishou Rinroku's library,

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:12.170
any book would increase in value.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.450
You haven't been putting them up for auction, have you?

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:26.080
Hey, let me examine how this fake emblem was made...

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.490
Rie...?

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:34.670
"The usual place"...

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.260
Yajima-san is... Hey...

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.370
Last year, you went out a number of times running errands for father, didn't you?

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:46.640
At those times, didn't you say you were going to Yajima-san's residence?

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:50.610
Why yes, I believe it was a friend of his who had just entered prison;

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.320
I went to deliver toys to his children.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.950
Were the only people there his wife and children?

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:56.820
Yes.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.280
Was his wife pretty?

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.860
Just forget it...

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.630
Kaishou Rinroku says that it's not his book...

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:15.020
What are your thoughts? As a detective, that is...

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:18.180
Something seems terribly suspicious.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.200
Suspicious?

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.060
If a book you had no recollection of selling suddenly appeared on the market,

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.430
the first thing you would usually do it suspect theft.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:28.810
But supposedly he didn't seem concerned in the slightest.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.200
What do you think?

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:32.940
Yajima-san.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:37.240
When you came to me, you'd already solved the code, hadn't you?

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.750
"I'll be at the usual place"..., right?

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:43.240
I assumed it was a letter summoning Kaishou Rinroku...

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.370
...and from a woman at that...

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:52.380
Pretend to be borrowing and lending books, then sneak codes within each of them;

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:57.880
I can only guess that the two people were
collaborating which books they would exchange.

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:01.510
In other words, this copy was originally from my own home.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:06.120
Then the person who wrote the code on your writing paper was...

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:09.520
Who's there?

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:11.650
Is someone in here?

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.530
It's me!

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.460
Haven't I been telling you that I'm home now?

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:17.640
Oh...

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:18.410
Darling!

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:22.620
I'm in the middle of some work. Go get some rest.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.750
Good, be careful on your way back.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:30.240
How long has your wife been blind?

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:32.960
It happened while I was in the correctional centre...

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:36.210
...along with our children going missing.

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:37.840
Your children?

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:40.340
It was suspected that they were kidnapped...

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:43.220
...but my wife went running off to look for them.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:48.060
Back then, even in this area, there were terrorist attacks from anti-government organizations.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:56.400
When my wife returned, she had lost the light of her eyes and her memories of the incident were vague and uncertain.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:02.480
Following that, my wife called a used book shop and had almost all of my books taken away...

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:07.040
...and all of the pictures our children drew ended up just as you've seen them.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.540
It's as if she thought she'd be able to forget everything.

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:14.540
This book might have very well been sold from my home.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.610
And what about your children?

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.380
It seems they were never found.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.050
It's nearly been a year since.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.860
When you sleep with a woman, which side do you sleep on?

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:29.430
Huh?

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:33.020
Are you sleeping with that R.A.I.?

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:40.780
Takako always laid along my right side...

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:43.190
...for as long as we've been together.

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:45.120
I'm left handed.

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:50.000
But after I returned, she would sleep on my left side, my right side...

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:54.250
I thought it was because she'd lost her sight, but eventually I realised...

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:58.380
Kaishou Rinroku is right handed.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.130
What are you doing?

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.770
Kazamori said she wanted to look at the camera.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:12.620
Hey, don't throw me!

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.160
Is that the R.A.I. from before?

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.050
So?

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:17.730
I infiltrated the footage found in the surveillance camera.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:20.950
At least six times in the previous year,

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:24.860
Kaishou Rinroku's car was parked outside this house.

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:27.120
I see.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:28.780
Wait a minute!

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:34.370
Even if she developed that kind of relationship with Rinroku, I don't feel like I can blame her.

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:41.000
I stuck firmly to my beliefs and ended up in prison for three years.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.010
But the children...

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:44.760
Yajima-san?

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:50.350
If Takako, in order to be with Rinroku, did something to keep the children from disturbing her...

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.440
I'll find out where your children are!

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.650
We can consider that your real request.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:01.410
No... You've already done what I hired you for.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:06.860
The souls in this house are about to burst free!

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:09.990
Let me ask her... That woman...

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.240
What do you want to ask?

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.700
What else?

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:16.460
"Where are your children?!"

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.320
Do you think that she killed them? Their own mother?

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:24.260
Kaishou might even have helped her!

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:28.670
If that were to be true, then all of the lies
and truths that he's been piling up...

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:30.850
...the entirety of his soul would be laid bare.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.320
Isn't that what you want?

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.520
Get away from me!

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:35.570
What's that?

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:36.650
Coloured pencil.

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:37.950
A tool used to draw pictures on paper.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:38.520
Hey!

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:41.390
Pictures?! I'm gonna draw! I'm gonna draw!

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:43.150
What should I draw on?

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:44.260
Geez... What are you, a kid?

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:44.260
Drawing paper, probably.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.990
Drawing paper? What's that?

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.450
Kazamori.

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:55.010
What was used to write this?

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:55.680
Why?

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:56.500
Just answer me.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:59.310
Man, you're such a slave driver.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.700
Pigment and wax...

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:07.650
The composition of an average coloured pencil.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.100
Where's the nearest used book store?

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.170
I'm not a GPS!

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:14.480
Answer me!

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.060
Roger...

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:30.660
Sorry!

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:36.380
Every single one of Yajima-san's books?

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:38.750
Yes, we took them all in.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:42.490
They were all fine items, so they sold easily as a set.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:43.810
Who bought them?

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:45.250
That's personal information...

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.510
Could you do something about it?

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:50.490
I can't! If I did that, I'd be the one getting arrested!

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.390
If you're looking for my father, he's not here!

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:57.650
Then I came at the right time.

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:58.890
I came with a request.

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:03.190
Please stop, Milady!

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.150
I'm the one who will be scolded for this.

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:06.350
Don't worry about it.

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:09.570
What... Could you possibly... Be you looking for?

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:14.380
Used books. Last year, Kaishou bought a
collection of books from a used book store.

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:18.030
They were all books sold from Yajima-san's residence.

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:20.110
If that's what you want, you won't find it there.

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:22.170
Over here.

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:27.050
These are all books too?

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.340
Another one?!

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:37.870
Tell me, Shinjuurou... does my father have
some kind of relation with Yajima-san's wife?

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.600
Shall we solve these together?

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:46.160
If you have the courage to do it, I'm sure you'll be able to find your answer.

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:01.040
Forgive me...

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:07.900
Akio... Kazuko...

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:13.550
You don't have to say a thing, Takako...

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:15.240
...I don't want to hear it.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.080
These are...

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:40.620
"I'll be waiting at the pool. July 10th, 3pm"...

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:44.370
"I have some sweets. Don't tell mum."

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.380
"Don't worry about mum".

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:53.010
"Let's play at the usual place. July 12th, 11am".

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:56.510
Akio! Kazuko!

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:01.010
Your children were using your books to play, sending coded messages to each other.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:06.650
Most likely, they were trying to not worry
their mother, who'd started acting strange.

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:09.650
Where might they be then?!

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:13.900
The answer to that was within the code as well.

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:19.410
This is a new play area that Kazuko-san found.

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:21.480
This place is...

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:23.910
It's a difficult thing to consider,

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:28.850
but there have been numerous incidents of
children being trapped in wreckage like this.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:33.920
Yajima-san?

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:38.430
No matter how long it takes me, I'll find them.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:41.370
I've kept them waiting for a year already...

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:57.700
It seems you've been hanging out with my daughter quite a bit.

00:17:58.480 --> 00:17:59.770
I'm Kaishou.

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:06.760
Was the reason you visited Yajima-san's residence so frequently...

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:09.570
...because his wife was acting so strangely?

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:12.090
Neglect.

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:15.730
There were signs of child neglect.

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:18.090
She stopped paying attention to the children,

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:20.470
and the older brother seemed to have been taking care of his sister.

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:23.350
She was lonely.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:27.600
After all, Takako-san really loved Yajima.

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:34.110
When the children first disappeared, she realised she'd done something terrible.

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:37.360
She blamed herself.

00:18:41.570 --> 00:18:44.370
When we received the report from Chairman Kaishou,

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:47.440
we took measures to prevent it from becoming an incident.

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:50.090
So you covered up the evidence of child abuse,

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:52.000
and as a result, the children's lives were...

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:56.000
The same way you covered up your own crime.

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:59.660
After people experience love a number of times,

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:02.290
aside from realising how boring it truly is,

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:05.210
they realise they are really none the wiser.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:10.280
As a result, they become unable to live without love.

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:15.940
Papa!

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:21.150
Uncle Kaishou!

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:23.160
Thank you!

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:27.810
Papa!

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:32.270
When I saw the slips of paper within the books Takako-san sold off,

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:34.370
I solved the code immediately.

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:35.800
It was so simple, after all.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:41.420
I then found the children pinned beneath a broken down vehicle.

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:44.440
Their lives weren't in danger,

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:46.180
but considering the mental state of their mother,

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:49.830
we held them in one of our child care facilities.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:51.510
Let me ask you one thing.

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:55.690
For what purpose do you reveal the truth?

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.690
For souls.

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:05.740
Is there really only one, consistent, truth?

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:08.080
What's wrong?

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:15.210
You exceeded my expectations...

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:21.780
Were you the one who imprinted Kaishou's
symbol onto the book you gave to Yajima-shi?

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:23.840
As to be expected from the "Defeated Detective".

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:28.350
Or maybe I should be calling you the "Great Detective".

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:30.950
Why do something like this?

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.330
I'm a novelist.

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:34.400
A novelist?

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:37.330
I write novels.

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:40.320
Not with a pen... but with reality.

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:42.820
Following the deductions of the "Great Detective",

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:44.610
all mysteries are brought to light!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:48.240
I expected that Yajima would kill his own wife.

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.100
Why would you try to make that happen?

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:54.710
Because that's the role of the "Great Detective".

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:57.730
No matter how cruel the outcome,

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:01.100
to wait until all of the victims have met their deaths, then bring forth his deduction:

00:21:01.100 --> 00:21:02.500
that is the "Great Detective".

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:06.940
No matter how tragic his reasons,

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:09.220
to expose everything in broad daylight;

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:10.140
that is the "Great Detective".

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.100
I have chosen you...

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:18.570
...as this world's final "Great Detective".

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:37.540
Wandering hazily on a pale morning, hearing a whispered prayer,

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:45.470
You and I trace a twisted scenery.

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:53.140
We're seeking the (truth). "We don't even care if it's a lie."

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:57.520
As if we can see right through it,

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:01.480
We follow it along.

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:05.440
Looking for, going beyond words,

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:09.450
Like a falling feather.

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:12.580
Looking for, find it,

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:18.920
So we can come closer together.

00:22:33.430 --> 00:22:37.430
Looking for, unravel it,

00:22:37.430 --> 00:22:41.440
Tear it apart, like a cloud.

00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:44.520
Looking for, find it,

00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:49.360
So we can come closer together.

00:22:51.530 --> 00:22:53.070
The next episode is inspired from:

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:56.900
Not "Meiji-era Ango Detective Stories" or even a mystery story at all!

00:22:56.900 --> 00:22:58.360
"The Retard"...?

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:01.250
Oh. But I figured we were gonna do this one.

00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:02.660
We'd better take this opportunity to do it now,

00:23:02.660 --> 00:23:05.590
since it's not a word you can really say on TV these days.

00:23:05.590 --> 00:23:06.560
"Retard", "Retard"!

00:23:06.560 --> 00:23:08.340
Oh, don't dub in like "idiot".

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:11.370
So anyway, it's not a mysterioso thing, but a war story.

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:12.930
How is this gonna be done?

00:23:12.930 --> 00:23:15.180
Next time on UN-GO: "Daydream".

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:16.770
Huh?! I'm not in the next episode?!

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:18.430
Hey! What's the deal with that?!

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:21.100
Hey! I wanna talk to someone in charge!
